  "dues": {
    "shareOfPay": 0.015,
    "citation": "Recalled from union constitutions and bylaws: UAW dues are 2.5 hours' straight-time pay per month since 2014 (about 1.44% of pay at 173 hours/month), many SEIU, AFSCME and UFCW locals set roughly 1.0-2.0% of base pay, building-trades locals combine flat monthly dues with 1-5% work assessments; summaries (e.g., Congressional Research Service, union LM-2 per-capita data) put typical dues near 1-2% of pay, often $40-$90 per month. Not opened in this session."
